      "side": 1,
      "message": "As is, this is a good check, so +1.\n\nAnother question is whether an extra byte should be allocated for the NUL byte.  sysconf(3) says:\n\n       HOST_NAME_MAX - _SC_HOST_NAME_MAX\n              Maximum length of a hostname, not including the terminating null\n              byte, as returned by gethostname(2).  Must not be  less than\n              _POSIX_HOST_NAME_MAX (255).\n\nSo, it seems like the allocation should include an extra byte and the overflow checks should switch from \u003e\u003d to \u003e.",
